/*
:name: xor_neg_one_unsigned_ctx
:type: equiv
*/
// A mixed-sign bitwise op with a non-negative result, inlined into an
// UNSIGNED enclosing expression. cgen emitted `a & (x ^ -1)` in its signed form
// (`$signed({1'b0,a}) & ($signed(..x..) ^ (1'sh1))`) and inlined it into the
// `| (c << s)`: the unsigned `c << s` made the whole Verilog expression
// unsigned, the 1-bit signed `-1` was ZERO-extended, and `x ^ -1` flipped only
// bit 0 -- a SILENT miscompile of the emitted Verilog (the LGraph was right).
// The Pyrope writer spells the regenerated `-x - 1` of Verilog's `~` as
// `x ^ -1` (user ruling 2026-09-29 (44)), so every round trip through it hit
// this (prp-v2prp2v-wrap_bitrange_dest, -comb_array_const_index_read).
pub mod xor_neg_one_unsigned_ctx(a:U8, b:U3, c:U8, s:U3) -> (o:U8@[0], p:U8@[0]) {
  wrap o = (a & ((b << s) ^ -1)) | (c << s)
  wrap p = (a ^ ((b << s) ^ -1)) | (c << s)
}
